{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED — pushed as Gerrit change 1633 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1633), commit ac8eb91a, branched from origin/main at 06335f71b (which already contains 1627, so no collision with the mutation session).\n\n## What landed in the change\n\n- scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py (new): pure summarize() rendering each non-successful job as TIMED OUT / CANCELLED / FAILED with its duration and html_url. Returns '' when everything succeeded, so a green run posts nothing.\n- .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml: two new steps in the vote job plus a key-cleanup step; 'checks: read' added; the trusted sparse-checkout now fetches the summarizer alongside the normalizer.\n- tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py (new, 22 tests), tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py (new, 11 tests).\n- tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port_heldout.py: one assertion updated, see below.\n\n## AC4 refined during implementation — please note the deviation\n\nAC4 as written expected a step using the action's 'comment-only: true' input. I did NOT use it. The action hardcodes MESSAGE=\"${STATUS}: <run url>\", and comment-only merely suppresses the labels — it posts the SAME canned text, so it cannot carry any detail. The comment is therefore posted with a direct 'ssh ... gerrit review <change>,<ps> --message ...' call carrying no --label, which is a comment-only review in Gerrit's own terms. The substance of AC4 (detail posted, no label cast) holds; the mechanism differs. Asserted by test_the_comment_step_casts_no_label, which greps the step for --label / Verified= / Code-Review=.\n\n## Observability-only, enforced by tests rather than asserted in prose\n\n- the cast step still reads vote-type: ${{ steps.normalize.outputs.vote-type }} (unchanged)\n- vote.needs is unchanged and pinned by a test\n- exactly one gerrit-review-action invocation exists in the vote job\n- both new steps are continue-on-error and run AFTER the cast, so if they break the vote is already on the change and the run cannot redden\n- the new steps are guarded on vote-type != 'success'\n\n## Security note\n\nThe summary reaches a remote 'gerrit review --message' over ssh inside single quotes, and job names are patchset-influenced (matrix shard names come from mutation-shards.toml). The summarizer strips ' and \\\\ and every control character except newline; three tests cover it, including a hostile shard name that tries to close the quote and append a command. The summarizer is fetched from the default branch via the existing trusted sparse-checkout, so the vote job still never executes patchset code.\n\n## Pre-existing test I had to touch\n\ntests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port_heldout.py::test_workflow_sparse_checkout_fetches_only_the_py asserted the literal line 'sparse-checkout: scripts/normalize_ci_conclusion.py'. The sparse-checkout is now a two-entry block, so I rewrote that assertion to parse the YAML and check the invariant it actually cared about: the normalizer is still named, every pattern is a .py file, and cone-mode is still false. Intent preserved, literal-string coupling removed.\n\n## Local gates\n\n835 passed, 1 skipped across tests/scripts/ + the workflow tests; scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py OK; make lint (ruff + zizmor + actionlint) and make typecheck both clean.\n\nWaiting on LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786514146768328001,"uuid":"d39a6272-33f6-4e23-9b99-47d10c0b453d"}